## Convert miles to km
121 \text{ miles} &= 121 \times 1.61
&= 194.81 \text{ km}
## Convert one hour to seconds
1 \text{ hour} &= 60 \times 60
&= 3600 \text{ seconds}
## Change km to metres
$1 \text{ km} = 1000 \text{ m}$.
194.81 \text{ km} &= 194.81 \times 1000
&= 194\,810 \text{ m}
## Divide the metres by the seconds
\text{Speed} &= \frac{194\,810}{3600}
&= 54.1139
&= 54.11
ANSWER: 54.11 \text{ m/s}

## Split the first bracket into its two terms
Multiply the whole second bracket by $4x$, then by $-10\sqrt{x}$.
(4x - 10\sqrt{x})(2x + 5\sqrt{x} - 7) &= 4x(2x + 5\sqrt{x} - 7) - 10\sqrt{x}(2x + 5\sqrt{x} - 7)
## Multiply out $4x$ times the second bracket
4x(2x + 5\sqrt{x} - 7) &= 4x \times 2x + 4x \times 5\sqrt{x} - 4x \times 7
&= 8x^2 + 20x\sqrt{x} - 28x
## Multiply out $-10\sqrt{x}$ times the second bracket
-10\sqrt{x}(2x + 5\sqrt{x} - 7) &= -20x\sqrt{x} - 50\sqrt{x}\sqrt{x} + 70\sqrt{x}
$\sqrt{x} \times \sqrt{x} = x$, so $-50\sqrt{x}\sqrt{x} = -50x$.
&= -20x\sqrt{x} - 50x + 70\sqrt{x}
## Add the two results and collect like terms
&= 8x^2 + 20x\sqrt{x} - 28x - 20x\sqrt{x} - 50x + 70\sqrt{x}
The $x\sqrt{x}$ terms cancel, and $-28x - 50x = -78x$.
&= 8x^2 - 78x + 70\sqrt{x}
ANSWER: 8x^2 - 78x + 70\sqrt{x}

## Choose the quotient rule parts
u &= 3, \quad u' = 0
v &= 2x - 7, \quad v' = 2
## Substitute into the quotient rule
g'(x) &= \frac{v u' - u v'}{v^2}
&= \frac{(2x-7)(0) - (3)(2)}{(2x-7)^2}
## Simplify the numerator
&= \frac{0 - 6}{(2x-7)^2}
&= -\frac{6}{(2x-7)^2}
## Explain why there are no turning points
A turning point needs $g'(x) = 0$, but the numerator is $-6$, which is never $0$.
Also $(2x-7)^2 > 0$ for every $x$ in the domain ($x \ne 3.5$), so $g'(x) < 0$ always.
So $g'(x) \ne 0$ for all $x$ in the domain: $g$ has no local maximum or minimum points.
ANSWER: g'(x) = -\frac{6}{(2x-7)^2} < 0 \text{ for all } x \text{ in the domain, so there are no turning points}
